        WHY IT IS IN THIS BIB: it is the citation that justifies NOT using Van Looveren and
        Klaise's IM1/IM2 in their published form (see `vanlooveren2019prototypes'). Analysis
        and verbatim quotes:
        `external\_literature/findings/im1\_im2\_plausibility\_2026-08.md' section 5. Their
        documented failures: IM1 rewards tiny changes and is skewed by class-reconstruction
        difficulty; IM2 decreases monotonically as the instance shrinks toward its minimal
        value, so an almost-black image outscores a legible digit; on higher-complexity data
        both metrics ``get close to statistically insignificant'' across methods; and no
        pre-trained autoencoders exist, so absolute values are not comparable across
        publications. They partially rehabilitate IM1 as a METHOD-LEVEL AGGREGATE, which is a
        direct mismatch with a per-point plausibility use. Their proposed replacements (Label
        Variation Score, Oracle score) are image-classifier-shaped and inherit the class
        partition, so they do NOT rescue the transfer either.}
}

